  "body": "**Replaces #437** (opened from the old fork, which can no longer take pushes). Same head commit; nothing else changed.\n\n**Stacked on #433** (#417), which is on #432 (#416). Part of #363. The #418 work is bf3b0d58.\n\n## What changed\n- **The option:** `ThreadInfeed.repeat_each_depth`, off by default. Every pass above the root is followed by an identical copy: same tip depth, same lattice shift, same helix phase. So a repeat can never cut deeper or move. The finishing and spring passes at the root are not repeated.\n- **Alternating infeed:** the side flips once per depth, not per cut, so a repeat keeps its flank.\n- **G76 refuses it by name.** The record carries a `repeat_each_depth` flag, written to the stream as `REP 1` only when set, plus a `RepeatEachDepth` post property. `fanuc-lathe.cps` refuses with \"repeat each roughing depth is not a G76 cycle (the cycle cuts each depth once)\".\n- **Defaults are byte-identical:** the stamp adds one byte only when the flag is on, and no project key or stream word is written when it's off. No version rung.\n- **UI:** a \"Repeat each depth\" checkbox on the Passes tab, after Spring passes. Its tooltip says G32 only, that G76 refuses it, and that tooling makers recommend against routine spring passes.\n- `docs/decisions/418-thread-repeat-pass.md`\n\n## How tested\n- motion `turning_thread_infeed`, 10/10, including two new tests:\n  - every roughing depth is cut twice (0.4, 0.4, 0.8, 0.8, 1.1, 1.1, 1.2, 1.2) and the default is unchanged move for move;\n  - a repeat is the same pass under every method × schedule, and the verdict stays silent.\n- app:\n  - `turning_thread_infeed` 5/5: the toggle goes stale and back to OK, takes 3 then 5 plunges, with undo and redo; round-trip writes the key only when set;\n  - `lathe_post_g76_schedule` 5/5: G76 refuses the repeat; `REP 1` rides the stream; G32 posts 5 passes.\n- `turning_thread`, `lathe_post_g76`, `inverted_post`, `project_roundtrip` and the app lib pass. No golden changed.\n- `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` on cl, post, motion, app and ui is clean.\n- The only failure is the headless-GPU ui test (no adapter on this Mac).\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nGUI check and a lathe sim or machine run. There is a combined test kit for #416, #417 and #418.\n\nChangelog: Threading op: optional repeat of each roughing depth (G32 output; G76 refuses it by name) (#418)\n\nFixes #418\n\n## Screenshots (Passes tab)\n\nRendered headless (egui_kittest `Harness::render()` on lavapipe) through the real `pages::properties` code: a lathe, bar stock, the TD-1732-60 threading insert and one Threading op, Passes tab open. Before is upstream/main, so the after-shot also shows the stacked parents' rows (#516 infeed plan). After: the same plan as #516's after-shot (Flank 29.5°, Constant area, minimum depth 0.05 mm, finish allowance 0.03 mm, 1 spring pass) with **Repeat each depth** on - the new row this PR adds.\n\n| Before (upstream/main) | After (this PR) |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-518/passes-tab-before.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-518/passes-tab-after.png) |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
